# Customer Custom Element Types

This directory is for customer-defined element types that extend the out-of-the-box types.

Custom types can inherit from:
- xpository:core:base
- xpository:core:standard
- xpository:document:generic
- Any other custom types

## Example Custom Type

Create a file like `my-custom-type.json`:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "description": "Custom task element for project management",
  "x-xpository": {
    "namespace": "mycompany:project:task",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "displayName": "Project Task",
    "parent": "xpository:core:standard",
    "metadata": {
      "abstract": false,
      "category": "custom",
      "icon": "clipboard-list",
      "color": "#F59E0B"
    }
  },
  "required": ["title", "priority", "dueDate"],
  "properties": {
    "priority": {
      "type": "string",
      "x-indexed": true,
      "enum": ["low", "medium", "high", "critical"],
      "description": "Task Priorities. Value can be low, medium, high, or critical"
    },
    "assignee": {
      "type": "string",
      "x-indexed": true,
      "description": "Who the task is assigned to",
      "maxLength": 255
    },
    "dueDate": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date",
      "x-indexed": true,
      "description": "The date the task is due"
    }
  }
}
```

*Note*: Because this model inherits fomr the standard core model, it must declare the required properties from the parent model.

## Configuration

To load custom types from external filesystem locations, add to `application.properties`:

```properties
xpository.element-types.locations[2]=file:/opt/xpository/types/*.json
```
